      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We suspect that EAC may be timing out during communication. However, it would not be considered normal behavior if this issue were occurring in every user's environment.\n\nAccording to the VRChat debug log, the following message was recorded:\n\n-----\n\n2026.06.23 21:10:04 Debug      -  [Behaviour] Received executive message: \n\nThe VRChat Anti-Cheat system could not maintain a verified connection.\n\nYou may be experiencing internet problems.\n\nIf your connection seems OK, check status.vrchat.com for server issues.\n\nYou can also try verifying your installation and / or completely reinstall VRChat.\n\nIf the issue persists, contact our Support team at vrch.at/support\n\nAccording to the EAC anticheatlauncher.log , the following message was recorded:\n\n----------------\n\n[12:00:08:904] [Windows] [EAC Bootstrapper] [Info] [Connection] Connecting to URL: https://modules-cdn.eac-prod.on.epicgames.com/modules/a4a57ff548934dbeba0cc7c62cdf9f34/76151011566a4757ae955b380b05c378/win64\n\n[12:00:08:966] [Windows] [EAC Bootstrapper] [Info] [Connection] Connect result: No error (0) Response Code: 304 Destination IP: 3.164.110.94\n\n[12:00:08:966] [Windows] [EAC Bootstrapper] [Info] No update needed.\n\n[12:00:11:369] [Windows] [EAC Bootstrapper] [Info] Launcher finished with: 301, 'Easy Anti-Cheatのゲームへのロードが完了しました'.\n\n[12:00:11:369] [Windows] [EAC Bootstrapper] [Info] Successfully initialized the Easy Anti-Cheat module, waiting for game window to become visible.\n\n[12:00:11:369] [Windows] [EAC Bootstrapper] [Info] Unlocking the launch lock, allowing next game to launch to take place.\n\n----\n\nThere are no error messages in the EAC logs before or after the disconnection occurred.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
